Subject: Goldfish warnings count skipped copies; scryfall_named's default printing

Found after the gateway's 0.7.22 release (Mystic Forge 1.3.2-mag3):

- goldfish_run, goldfish_ab and goldfish_start warned "not recognized by
  Scryfall, skipped: Bera, Hamer" with names only, so a reader could not
  tell how many cards the simulation left out (two copies of a typo are two
  cards fewer in the library). goldfish_annotate already said "2 Bera"
  (patch 0004); the other three now say it too: "skipped: 2 Bera, 1 Hamer".
- scryfall_named with no set_code showed Scryfall's default printing, which
  is its newest: on 2026-10-11 "Swamp" was Marvel: Darkhold Destiny #296, a
  preview released 2027-04-09 with games: [] and no prices. It now shows the
  printing every other lookup uses when no set is named (patch 0005's
  _default_printing: the newest printing released by today that is sold on
  paper; one oracleid search, only when Scryfall's default is no good), and
  a line says which printing it is: "Printing: FDN #281, the newest printing
  out on paper. Pass set_code for another printing." With set_code the
  output is unchanged.
Tests: tests/test_goldfish_skipped_copies.py,
tests/test_named_default_printing.py.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 (main, 2026-10-04) has neither
fix, and no open pull request touches this code. Drop this patch when it
does. Needs patches 0004 and 0005 (it reuses 0005's _default_printing).

